OL,3,GNEWSAWhat does takeover by sportswear
OL,4,Afirm mean for traditional shoemaker?
OL,5,
OL,6,FTraditional shoemaker Grenson has been
OL,7,Fbought by international sportswear firm
OL,8,FCastore. But what does the move mean
OL,9,Ffor one of the most famous names in a
OL,10,Fcounty famed for its footwear heritage?
OL,12,FFor 160 years it has been making shoes
OL,13,Fand boots that have been worn by
OL,14,Fsoldiers in both world wars,
OL,15,Fcelebrities ` and even Doctor Who.
OL,17,FThe firm that became Grenson began in
OL,18,F1866 when William Green started making
OL,19,Fshoes in a loft above a corn merchant
OL,20,Fin Rushden, Northamptonshire.
OL,23,APub: 08-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
